-- report.talk: the syntax sketch's 09-http-fetch `summarise`, rewritten
-- against the stdlib outline (ADR 0021).

use average, unique from list
use pad, padLeft, join from text

on summarise station, readings
  put the temp of r for every r in readings into temps

  put average(temps) into mean     -- `list`, written in the language
  put max(temps) into warmest      -- Built-in: ambient, no `use` needed
  put round(mean, 1) into mean     -- Built-in, rounds half away from zero
  -- Was: put the average of temps into mean
  --      put the max of temps into warmest
  -- ADR 0021: `the p of x` is only for the structural property list, so
  -- aggregates are called `f(x)`. `average` needs a `use` line and `max`
  -- doesn't, because Guards need `max` and it has to be a Built-in.

  put the length of temps into n   -- a structural property, unchanged

  put unique(the wind of r for every r in readings) into winds
  tell log to write row(station, mean) & "  winds: " & join(winds, ", ")
end summarise

function row station, mean
  return pad(station, 8) & padLeft(mean as text, 6)
end row

-- Grouping is a Comprehension clause, left to a follow-up (ADR 0021):
--   put every r in readings grouped by the day of r into byDay
-- ?? That gives a map of lists keyed by day. Without it there's no
--    stdlib `group`: the language has no function values to pass one.
--
-- There is no `reduce` either. A loop does it:
--   put 0 into total
--   repeat for each r in readings
--     add the rain of r to total
--   end repeat
